1015.body:
The number field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_n)$ generated by a primitive $n$-th root of unity $\zeta_n = e^{2\pi i/n}$ is called a cyclotomic field . The Minimal Polynomial The minimal polynomial of $\zeta_n$ is the cyclotomic polynomial : $$\Phi_n(x) = \prod_{\substack{1 \le k \le n \ \gcd(k,n)=1}} \left(x - e^{2\pi i k/n}\right)$$ Its degree is $\varphi(n)$ (Euler's totient function). $\Phi_n$ is irreducible in $\mathbb{Q}[x]$. Examples : $\Phi_1(x) = x - 1$ $\Phi_2(x) = x + 1$ $\Phi_3(x) = x^2 + x + 1$ $\Phi_4(x) = x^2 + 1$ $\Phi_6(x) = x^2 - x + 1$ $\Phi_p(x) = x^{p-1} + x^{p-2} + \cdots + 1$ ($p$ prime) The cyclotomic polynomials satisfy $x^n - 1 = \prod_{d \mid n} \Phi_d(x)$ and can be computed factor by factor using Möbius inversion. Properties of the Field $[\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_n) : \mathbb{Q}] = \varphi(n)$. $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_n)$ is an Abelian extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ (its Galois group is $(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z})^*$). Its ring of integers is $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta_n]$; the discriminant depends on the prime factors of $n$. Example : the extension degree of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_5)$ is $\varphi(5) = 4$, with minimal polynomial $\Phi_5(x) = x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1$. Elements are represented as $a_0 + a_1\zeta + a_2\zeta^2 + a_3\zeta^3$ ($a_i \in \mathbb{Q}$). In oCAS, constructing a cyclotomic field only requires specifying the cyclotomic polynomial: use ocas_domain::{AlgebraicNumberField, Domain, Rational, RationalDomain}; // Q(ζ_5): minimal polynomial x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1
// ascending powers: [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
let field = AlgebraicNumberField::new( RationalDomain, vec![ Rational::new(1, 1), Rational::new(1, 1), Rational::new(1, 1), Rational::new(1, 1), Rational::new(1, 1), ],
);
let zeta = field.alpha(); // ζ_5
// ζ_5^5 = 1 (guaranteed by the minimal polynomial)
let z5 = field.pow(&zeta, 5);
assert_eq!(z5, field.one());

