When $m(x) \bmod p$ is reducible over $\mathbb{F}_p$, the ring $\mathbb{F}_p[x]/(m)$ is not a field — it has zero divisors. oCAS does not verify irreducibility of the minimal polynomial and allows constructing the ring modulo a reducible modulus. In that case: inv returns None for non-zero zero divisors (the extended Euclidean algorithm gives $\gcd \ne 1$). gcd_anf skips such primes (the min_poly_irreducible_mod check). Example : $m(x) = x^2 - 1 = (x-1)(x+1)$ is reducible over $\mathbb{Q}$. The ring $\mathbb{Q}[x]/(x^2-1)$ has the zero divisor $\alpha - 1$ (since $(\alpha-1)(\alpha+1) = \alpha^2-1 = 0$). let field = AlgebraicNumberField::new( RationalDomain, vec![Rational::new(-1, 1), Rational::new(0, 1), Rational::new(1, 1)],
);
let alpha = field.alpha();
let a = field.sub(&alpha, &field.one());
assert!(field.inv(&a).is_none()); // α − 1 is a zero divisor

