Signature : pub fn determinant(&self) -> Result<D::Element, MatrixError> Function : Computes the determinant of a square matrix using the Bareiss fraction-free algorithm (with partial pivoting). Algorithm highlights : Reduces the matrix to upper triangular form by elimination, dividing at each step by the previous pivot (Bareiss guarantees exact divisibility) Partial pivoting: when a zero pivot is encountered, searches downward for a nonzero row and swaps If an entire column becomes zero during elimination, the determinant is zero The sign is determined by the parity of the number of row swaps Return value : Ok(det) — the determinant Err(MatrixError::ShapeMismatch) — the matrix is not square Example : use ocas_domain::{Integer, IntegerDomain};
