Signature : pub fn solve_diophantine(a: i64, b: i64, c: i64) -> Option<DiophantineSolution> Description : Solves the linear Diophantine equation $ax + by = c$ using the extended Euclidean algorithm. A solution exists if and only if $\gcd(a, b) \mid c$. Parameters : Parameter Type Description a i64 The coefficient of $x$ b i64 The coefficient of $y$ c i64 The constant on the right-hand side Returns : Option<DiophantineSolution> Some(sol): the particular/general solution structure when a solution exists None: $\gcd(a, b) \nmid c$; the equation has no integer solution Errors : does not return a Result; returns None when unsolvable. Example : use ocas_calc::solve::solve_diophantine; // Solve 3x + 5y = 1
// Particular solution: x = 2, y = -1 (since 3×2 + 5×(-1) = 1)
// General solution: x = 2 + 5k, y = -1 - 3k
let sol = solve_diophantine(3, 5, 1).unwrap();
assert_eq!(sol.particular, (2, -1));
assert_eq!(sol.general, (5, -3)); // No solution: 2x + 4y = 3 (gcd(2,4)=2 does not divide 3)
assert!(solve_diophantine(2, 4, 3).is_none()); See also : solve_linear_integer

