assert!(rule.apply(&ctx, z).is_none()); Rule::apply pub fn apply(&self, ctx: &AtomArena<'a>, atom: Atom<'a>) -> Option<Atom<'a>> Function : Attempts to apply the rule to an atom. Returns Some(replacement result) when the pattern matches and the condition holds, otherwise None. Parameters : Parameter Type Description ctx &AtomArena<'a> The expression arena context atom Atom<'a> The target expression Return value : Option<Atom<'a>> — Some means the rule was applied, None means no match or the condition failed. See also : match_pattern, simplify

