Signature : pub fn legendre(a: &Integer, p: &Integer) -> i8 Description : Computes the Legendre symbol $\left(\frac{a}{p}\right)$. Parameters : Parameter Type Description a &Integer The integer under test p &Integer An odd prime (primality is guaranteed by the caller) Return value : Value Meaning 1 $a$ is a quadratic residue (QR) modulo $p$ -1 $a$ is a quadratic non-residue (QNR) modulo $p$ 0 $p \mid a$ Note : primality of p is guaranteed by the caller; the function is internally equivalent to jacobi(a, p). Example : use ocas_domain::Integer;
