Signature : pub fn dlog_bsgs(base: &Integer, target: &Integer, modulus: &Integer) -> Option<Integer> Description : Solves $base^x \equiv \text{target} \pmod{\text{modulus}}$ with the baby-step giant-step (BSGS) algorithm, searching $x < \text{modulus}$. Parameters : Parameter Type Description base &Integer The base target &Integer The target value modulus &Integer The modulus Return value : Option<Integer> — Some(x) with $0 \leq x < \text{modulus}$, or None if no solution exists. Error conditions : $\gcd(\text{base}, \text{modulus}) \neq 1$ (the base is not a unit). No such $x$ exists. Complexity : $O(\sqrt{\text{modulus}})$ time and space. Only suitable for small modulus. Implementation details : a HashMap stores the baby steps; giant-step lookups take $O(\sqrt{m})$. Example : use ocas_domain::Integer;
use ocas_domain::number_theory::dlog::dlog_bsgs; // 2 is a primitive root mod 11; 2^7 = 128 ≡ 7 (mod 11)
