pub fn reorder<O2: MonomialOrder>(&self) -> GroebnerBasis<D, O2>
where D: 'static, Description : Changes the monomial order of the Gröbner basis. Reinterprets the polynomials under the target order and re-runs F4. This is the simple order-change path; for zero-dimensional ideals, use fglm for the faster $O(n \cdot D^3)$ conversion. Type parameters : Parameter Description O2 Target monomial order Returns : GroebnerBasis<D, O2> — a Gröbner basis under the target order. Example : use ocas_domain::{RationalDomain, Rational};
