pub fn fglm<D: Domain, O2: MonomialOrder>( gb: &GroebnerBasis<D, impl MonomialOrder>,
) -> Option<GroebnerBasis<D, O2>> Description : The FGLM order-change algorithm (Faugère–Gianni–Lazard–Mora 1993). Converts a Gröbner basis of a zero-dimensional ideal from one monomial order to another, with complexity $O(n \cdot D^3)$ ($D$ is the vector space dimension of $R/I$), much faster than re-running F4 for large zero-dimensional ideals. Algorithm steps : Compute the staircase — the set of monomials not divisible by any leading monomial Traverse the staircase monomials in the target order For each monomial, compute its normal form under the current basis If the normal form is linearly dependent on the vectors seen so far, construct a new basis element from the coefficient relation Otherwise, add it to the set of seen vectors Parameters : Parameter Type Description gb &GroebnerBasis<D, impl MonomialOrder> The input Gröbner basis (must be reduced) Returns : Option<GroebnerBasis<D, O2>> — Some(gb) is the converted basis; None means the ideal is not zero-dimensional (the staircase is infinite). Example : use ocas_domain::{RationalDomain, Rational};
use ocas_poly::sparse::{Grevlex, Lex};
use ocas_poly::{GroebnerBasis, SparseMultivariatePolynomial, f4};
