pub fn is_zero_dimensional(gb: &GroebnerBasis<RationalDomain, Lex>) -> bool Description : Checks whether the ideal is zero-dimensional. The ideal is zero-dimensional if and only if for every variable $x_i$ some leading monomial in the GB is a pure power $x_i^N$ (equivalently, the staircase/set of standard monomials is finite). Parameters : Parameter Type Description gb &GroebnerBasis<RationalDomain, Lex> A Lex-order Gröbner basis over the rationals Returns : bool — true if zero-dimensional. Example : use ocas_domain::{RationalDomain, Rational};
