The content of a polynomial $f = \sum a_i x^i \in \mathbb{Z}[x]$ is defined as the GCD of its coefficients: $$\text{cont}(f) = \gcd(a_0, a_1, \ldots, a_n)$$ The primitive part is defined as: $$\text{pp}(f) = f / \text{cont}(f)$$ Gauss's lemma : the product of two primitive polynomials is again primitive. It follows that: $$\gcd(f, g) = \gcd(\text{cont}(f),, \text{cont}(g)) \cdot \gcd(\text{pp}(f),, \text{pp}(g))$$ This allows the content (an integer GCD) and the primitive part (a polynomial GCD) to be computed separately. In oCAS: use ocas_poly::DenseUnivariatePolynomial;
